Subject: Plug-in: CoreAnimation's pipelines as it asks for them, its luma_boost drawn, memoryless told to the core

What the frame traces of the home and of an app opening show the plug-in doing
otherwise than asked, each put right:

A pipeline CoreAnimation makes at run time (one its pipeline library does not
name; its functions come labelled, com.apple.coreanimation.frag.<constants>)
was compiled from "the nearest variant" of the library: another function, with
other constants -- TimgA2S1Xhf_Ixrg as ..Xhfcx_Ixrg, TmuaA2S1Xhf_Ixrg_Isqr as
..Xhfcx_Isrc_Isqr, TimgBdsoA2Xhfn_Isrc as ..Xhfcn_Isrc, eight of them in one
trace of the home. Such a pipeline is now compiled from the functions' own
modules with the constants CoreAnimation gave them (hm_function_constants),
which is what Metal asks; the library's variants are used where they are the
same function by CoreAnimation's own names (the function's label, or a pipeline
of the library by its label), and both stages of a pipeline are of one making.
Only when the compiler refuses what was asked is the nearest variant compiled
in its place, with a line that says so and why (the window server aborts on a
render pipeline that fails twice); metal_strict gives the refusal instead.

luma_boost was left out of every frame (the last draw of each main pass: the
picture's luminance through a LUT, read back by framebuffer fetch), from when
the library handed to the window server was another system's. This system's
library has its own, and it is drawn. The stand-ins for functions "the library
lacks" (luma_boost and edr_scale as inplace_copy, which writes a texture from
a draw and was refused) are gone with it: the functions asked for are the ones
compiled.

A texture asked for with MTLStorageModeMemoryless is told to the core
(hakios_metal_texture_set_memoryless). The passes: lines and the trace's gpass
lines say which attachments each tiled pass wrote, read, loaded and stored.


